# Ensure shell scripts always use LF line endings
*.sh text eol=lf

# Ensure PowerShell scripts use consistent line endings across platforms
*.ps1 text eol=lf

# The reference profile and its checksum sidecar are hashed BYTE-EXACT
# (AB#735, T1 AB#732 §1), so their bytes must be identical on every platform.
# Without this, git's autocrlf normalizes profile.json to CRLF on a Windows
# checkout, the embedded resource carries different bytes than the sidecar
# pins, and the integrity check fails for every Windows user — verified, not
# theorized: CI hashed the CRLF form to 6d747175… against the LF pin d2cf4c20…
#
# `text eol=lf` rather than `-text` on purpose: these stay diffable text, which
# T1 §1 explicitly requires ("reviewing a profile change in a PR must remain a
# diff of a human-readable file"), while the working tree is forced to LF
# everywhere.
src/Twig.Infrastructure/Resources/ReferenceProfile/profile.json text eol=lf
src/Twig.Infrastructure/Resources/ReferenceProfile/profile.json.sha256 text eol=lf
